Secrets And Auth

Purpose

Reference this file when the git skill needs to explain or detect GitHub/GitLab authentication.

Supported paths

- Secrets Manager may store GitHub and GitLab tokens.
- GitHub CLI can authenticate through a browser sign-in flow.
- GitLab CLI or provider-specific tooling can authenticate through token or browser-supported flows where available.

Rules

- Detect existing auth before asking the user to configure new auth.
- Never print, paste, or commit token values.
- Prefer provider CLI auth for interactive setup when available.
- Use Secrets Manager when scripts or non-interactive workflows need stored tokens.
- If both GitHub and GitLab are configured, explain which remote each command will affect before pushing or pulling.

Details belong here, not in `SKILL.md`, so the top-level git skill stays short.
